# Git Pull — Sync From GitHub

## Trigger phrases

Activate when the user says: **pull**, **sync from GitHub**, **get latest**, **update from remote**, or similar.

Default target branch is **`development`**. Pull **`main`** only when they ask for stable/production.

Pair with **Git-Push-Development-Rule** when they ask to sync both directions.

---

## Policy

- **Default sync branch: `development`**
- **`main`** only when user requests production/stable baseline
- **Never discard local work silently** — check `git status` before and after

**Remote:** `origin` → `https://github.com/WillMoose23/vibecoded-pokemon-engine.git`

---

## Pre-pull checks (parallel)

```bash
cd /Users/rheyn/Desktop/project
git status
git branch -vv
git remote -v
git fetch origin
```

Report: current branch, uncommitted changes, ahead/behind vs `origin`.

**Uncommitted changes:** stash or commit first; ask user if unclear.

---

## Pull development (default)

```bash
git fetch origin
git checkout development
git pull origin development --no-rebase
```

If `origin/development` does not exist, tell the user and offer to create it.

---

## Pull main (user requested only)

```bash
git fetch origin
git checkout main
git pull origin main --no-rebase
```

Return to `development` afterward unless user wants to stay on `main`.

---

## After pull

1. `git status` — summarize commits/files changed
2. If code changed, run:
   ```bash
   make test
   python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -q
   ```
3. On merge conflicts: list files and stop; resolve with user

---

## Sync both branches (optional)

When user asks to sync everything:

```bash
git fetch origin
git checkout main && git pull origin main --no-rebase
git checkout development && git pull origin development --no-rebase
```

---

## Forbidden without explicit user request

- `git reset --hard`, `git clean -fd`, force-push, auto-merge to `main`, open PRs without asking
